messages:
alexa (appsec): heads up — nightly SAST on `infra/` spiked, ~30 new HIGH findings. most of them are from the code that touches keystore access. failing decrypts in CI logs. :eyes;

mike (infra): ugh. any error samples? stack / logs?;

alexa (appsec): sample from gha job `sast-runner-04`:
``
2026-03-22T03:17:12Z ERROR keystore: decrypt failed key=projects/redwood/locations/global/keyRings/keystore/cryptoKeys/main reason=permission_denied
2026-03-22T03:17:12Z SAST scanner: open file infra/keystore/client.go: line 57: potential priv escalation (high)
2026-03-22T03:17:12Z CI: retrying decrypt (1/3)
```
looks like scanner tried to load files and we got KMS permission_denied.;

sara (sre): sec-bot just created an incident? @sec-bot can you dump the incident id?;

sec-bot: Incident created: INC-20260322-1182. Pager duty notified.;

mike (infra): we rolled a small RBAC change to `roles/keystore-access` binding yesterday afternoon for a service account used by `gha-runner-sa`. possible regression. i can check IAM bindings.;

vinh (devex): the scanner runs as `scanner-runner@redwood-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com` — that SA needs `cloudkms.cryptoKeyVersions.useToDecrypt` on the key. did that binding get removed?;

mike (infra): checking now...;

mike (infra): confirmed: binding for `scanner-runner@...` was removed during a cleanup PR (PR #3721) that consolidated ephemeral runners. the policy change was meant to be safe but we missed this SA.;

alexa (appsec): that explains fail -> findings noise. two things: 1) suppress the noisy alerts so we don't triage duplicates, 2) re-add permission or add a scoped proxy so scanner can read without direct key perms.;

sara (sre): oncall handoff: i'll temporarily grant the SA a narrow decrypt role and watch CI. will document in incident.;

mike (infra): patching IAM now:
``
gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding redwood-infra \
  --member=serviceAccount:scanner-runner@redwood-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \
  --role=roles/cloudkms.cryptoKeyDecrypter
```
rolled.;

sec-bot: IAM binding change detected by auditlog watcher: AUDIT-LOG-7091.;

alexa (appsec): re-run the nightly SAST or at least re-process the queue so the scanner can re-evaluate those files. we should avoid mass auto-suppressions.;

vinh (devex): kicked a manual re-run: `/run-scan infra --type sast --since 2026-03-21T00:00`;

sara (sre): scanner started, I'll tail logs. if findings drop, we mark as false positives from decrypt failure.;

mike (infra): quick note — audit logs show the binding removal happened at 2026-03-21T18:04 by svcacct-cleanup (bot). adding a follow-up ticket to tighten the cleanup rule.;

alexa (appsec): also noticed a mismatch between scanner metadata and keystore audit entries: scanner asserts key version v3 used, while KMS audit shows v2. could be caching from the runner image — worth investigating but lower priority than getting CI green.;

vinh (devex): noted — scanner image may have cached a local vendor file. i'll check the scanner container startup script to ensure it doesn't pin old KMS versions or keys.;

sara (sre): re-run results: 3 new HIGH remain (actual code issues), 27 cleared as scanner decryption errors.;

alexa (appsec): good. thanks. for the 27 cleared — i will mark them as noise and close with note "CI decrypt failure, upstream IAM change". i'll attach audit log snippet and incident id.;

mike (infra): action items: 1) add an automated check in cleanup bot to ignore SAs whose names match scanner/runners; 2) add a preflight IAM diff on infra PRs that touch keystore bindings; 3) create a short runbook for this class of failure. i'll own 1+2.;

vinh (devex): i'll update scanner image startup to verify KMS key/version via `gcloud kms keys versions describe` to fail fast with clear error. small PR incoming.;

alexa (appsec): and i'll update triage playbook: if >80% of findings from a run have identical stack trace pointing at keystore decrypt, auto-open an incident and annotate findings as "likely infra decrypt noise" before human triage. reduces churn.;

sara (sre): oncall: I'll keep monitoring for next 4 hours and will escalate if we see errors. handing off to night oncall @mike if issue recurs. :thumbsup;

sec-bot: Incident INC-20260322-1182 status: RESOLVED by policy rollback & IAM patch. Linked ticket: TKT-4579.;

alexa (appsec): filing two follow-ups: TKT-4579 (cleanup bot whitelist + preflight checks) and TKT-4580 (scanner startup KMS verification). tagging owners.;

mike (infra): closing thread. thanks team. :party_parrot;
